WEBVTT

00:10:56.694 --> 00:11:00.572
it helps to pay attention
to its quantum classification.

00:11:00.572 --> 00:11:04.493
So all particles come
in one of two quantum categories,

00:11:04.535 --> 00:11:06.036
fermions and bosons.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.415
So fermions, even when things get cold,

00:11:09.415 --> 00:11:11.542
like to keep their distance
from each other.

00:11:11.542 --> 00:11:13.210
They're antisocial.

00:11:13.252 --> 00:11:14.795
That's how it is.

00:11:14.837 --> 00:11:16.171
Bosons, on the other hand,

00:11:16.213 --> 00:11:18.632
when they get below
a critical temperature,

00:11:18.632 --> 00:11:21.135
they're like five-year-olds
on a soccer field,

00:11:21.176 --> 00:11:23.220
so they don't have a concept of formation,

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.097
they just bunch up together.

00:11:26.515 --> 00:11:28.142
So in technical terms,

00:11:28.142 --> 00:11:31.353
we call this the formation
of a Bose-Einstein condensate,